  '13#ג': `Beginning of sighting. All Acharonim agree Rama though requires study — no dispute found — Beit Yosef innovated from above siman 184 if veset extended days we follow veset beginning only concerned beginning — Rama decided since we rule thus siman 184 beginning; appears per their words difficulty Tur contradicts — above brought father holds only concerned beginning sighting; here concludes like Ramban concerned equal veset too — certainly Tur holds stam beginning sighting essence days subsidiary open following; stam women; but saw fifteenth month three four days then sixteenth seventeenth — skip veset uncommon equal common — why say skip veset not equal veset — end only fourteenth month not skip only sometimes preceded similar sighting mere blood addition; unlike equal veset always follow beginning cannot say beginning mere addition; Bach supported Raavad Ba'al HaNefesh also only concerned beginning sighting — Raavad no proof — he holds no establishment niddah days — if ruled between fifteenth seventeenth no equal veset no establishment niddah days — Raavad all concern lest flowed together — main sight seventeenth fifteenth preceded mere addition; Raavad admits if sight without pause would establish equal veset — considers stam not flowed only paused — here veset niddah days — for us rule establishment niddah days plainly establishes — law requires study who disputes Tur Ramban without proof — end quote.`,
