  '17#_': `Like unfixed veset — if happened twice so Shach s.k. 48 — appears Raavad view above seif 7 seif 3 if established hour veset i.e. immersion act like jumps — learns woman saw ascending immersion — therefore uprooted one hour even without examination but begins concerned for her hour — since presumed concerned initially like unfixed veset; here too if jumps though not aligned days nevertheless aligned hours — initially need only concern that hour if jumped that hour — not before after; Mechaber abbreviated relied above seif 3; appears Ran Niddah chiddushim disputes — how permit this woman relations on river always sees ascending immersion — resolve like jump veset not established; challenge nevertheless begins concerned like unfixed since accustomed see — likewise not this view; Maggid Mishnah resolves Raavad special hour commanded relations before that hour; these matters disputed; Shach s.k. that if composite days jumps concerned veset arrived jumped even not established three times need not elaborate — clear Ba'al HaNefesh; if not jumped that day no concern not say perhaps establish days alone like other body veset; Perishah s.k. 59 seems also concerned — perhaps wrote per Tur holds established jump veset alone — equal jump veset to other body veset; for us difference establishment alone perhaps divide.`,
  '2#_': `Four sightings are required, etc. One may challenge: veset ha-chodesh and veset ha-shavua are one in law, and we learn veset ha-chodesh from veset ha-shavua as explicit in the Gemara; if so plainly veset ha-dilug applies to both as to veset ha-chodesh. See Tosafot Bava Kamma 34 regarding the goring ox — likewise explicit. If so, for the view that we rule like Rav that two skips suffice and these are veset ha-chodesh — three sightings — likewise for veset ha-shavua. Example: a woman saw first on Sunday the 1st, at end of day 20 saw again on Friday the 6th, at end of twenty saw on Wednesday the 4th — behold three sightings and two skips in two days that are equal skips — behold veset ha-shavua for skip like veset ha-chodesh for skip. I wonder why the Acharonim did not notice this. My resolution: how can one say she established veset for skipping and veset ha-shaveh? We say it is more reasonable she established the equal veset since a woman rarely establishes veset for skip; therefore we say she is not concerned for skip until she establishes it three times. If so, truly when she saw three times with a thirty-day interval of two days she established veset ha-shavua in skip — only when she adds a fourth sighting at end of twenty. If so there are two types of veset here — either interval veset which is the equal veset, or veset ha-shavua in skip; Shulchan Aruch's intent is it is not established for interval until four times and then it is interval veset and not skip veset for the week. If difficulty: what difference — in either case she must forever be concerned for day twenty? Answer: if she saw in her youth or one onah passed and she did not see — if you judge this veset ha-shavua for skip, nevertheless at its time she is concerned for it is equal in law to veset ha-chodesh and there is no difference whether she sees in youth or one onah passed; but if we judge it for interval veset, if one onah she does not see at its time she is not concerned in youth — then interval is void and no concern as below. And further:`,
